WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.836 --> 00:00:03.604
- [Voiceover] They dance, they
flail, they're a big wacky

00:00:03.604 --> 00:00:05.308
and awkward way to get your attention.

00:00:05.308 --> 00:00:07.024
But did you know these Tall Boys debuted

00:00:07.024 --> 00:00:09.441
at the 1996 Olympics, as art?

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:14.789
(lighthearted Caribbean music)

00:00:14.789 --> 00:00:17.500
Meet Peter Minshall, a
prominent Caribbean artist.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.908
Known in Trinidad as the
creator of larger than life

00:00:19.908 --> 00:00:22.436
dancing puppets created for Carnival.

00:00:22.436 --> 00:00:24.071
His work made its way to a book called

00:00:24.071 --> 00:00:25.483
Caribbean Festival Arts.

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:27.394
And that book made its way to a man.

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:30.220
A man on the steering
committee of the Olympics.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.500
Peter was commissioned to
help create an unforgettable

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.907
opening for the 1996
Olympic games in Atlanta.

00:00:35.907 --> 00:00:38.509
In a moment nothing short of pure genius,

00:00:38.509 --> 00:00:40.179
Peter returned to his roots by sketching

00:00:40.179 --> 00:00:41.679
a puppet-like structure

00:00:41.679 --> 00:00:44.515
but this time he turned it
into an inflatable air-man

00:00:44.515 --> 00:00:47.500
that would move and dance
just like his manned-puppets.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.454
For this he had to call in another artist,

00:00:49.454 --> 00:00:52.227
Doron Gazit, an engineer
who happened to be obsessed

00:00:52.227 --> 00:00:53.837
with anything inflatable.

00:00:53.837 --> 00:00:55.465
Between both men they
were able to accomplish

00:00:55.465 --> 00:00:57.550
the seemingly impossible:

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:01.214
60 foot inflatable two-legged dancing men.

00:01:01.214 --> 00:01:03.700
The Tall Boys were nothing
short of a success.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.183
After they graced the
Olympics, Gazit got a patent

00:01:06.183 --> 00:01:08.595
and licensed the design
to various advertisers.

00:01:08.595 --> 00:01:10.643
Now they're everywhere.

00:01:10.643 --> 00:01:13.011
Used car lots, cropped
fields, shopping centers,

00:01:13.011 --> 00:01:14.692
you name it.

00:01:14.692 --> 00:01:17.969
So the next time you see a big
ridiculous inflated Tall Boy

00:01:17.969 --> 00:01:19.431
waving at you in the distance,

00:01:19.431 --> 00:01:21.217
just imagine you're in the Caribbean

00:01:21.217 --> 00:01:23.163
dancing along to the drum beat.

00:01:23.163 --> 00:01:27.080
(lighthearted Caribbean music)

